🧠 Analytics Methodology
1️⃣ Feature Engineering

              From monthly aggregated product–country sales, the following features were engineered:
              
              Total sales amount
              
              Total boxes shipped
              
              Transaction count
              
              Log-based month-over-month growth
              
              Log-based 3-month growth
              
              Rolling 3-month volatility
              
              Log growth was used instead of percentage growth to stabilise extreme base-rate distortions.

2️⃣ Opportunity Score

              Each product–country combination is scored monthly using a weighted composite index:
              
              0.45 × Sales Volume
              0.25 × Momentum (MoM Log Growth)
              0.20 × 3-Month Log Growth
              0.10 × Stability (Inverted Volatility)


              Scores are normalised within each month to allow relative comparison.
              
              The highest score in each month receives:
              
                  opportunity_rank = 1
                  Lower rank number = stronger marketing opportunity.

3️⃣ Key Modelling Decisions

              Log transformation applied to growth metrics to prevent extreme distortion.
              
              Minimum activity threshold applied to avoid ranking low-volume anomalies.
              
              Volatility penalty included to reduce influence of unstable spikes.
              
              Ranking performed per month to maintain contextual comparability.

📊 Dashboard Outputs
              Executive Sales Overview
              
              KPI Cards (Total Sales, Boxes, Transactions)
              
              Sales Trend Analysis
              
              Country-level performance
              
              Product Analytics
              
